What are Air Dome Structures?
Air Dome Structures are lightweight, flexible architectural solutions constructed from high-performance fabric membranes. These innovative structures utilize continuous air pressure to maintain their shape, offering advantages such as rapid deployment, cost efficiency, and versatility across applications. Common configurations include single-layer and multi-layer designs, with materials typically featuring reinforced PVC or PTFE coatings for durability and weather resistance.
These structures are primarily used for creating large, clear-span enclosures for sports facilities, industrial storage, swimming pools, and event spaces. Their ability to be quickly installed and relocated makes them particularly valuable for temporary applications where traditional construction would be impractical or too expensive.
